craft ? Traveling at the speed of light, the answer is one day. In fact, the Voyager 1 spacecraft was confirmed to reach its one light-day distance milestone on November 18, at 10:16:07 UTC, nearly 50 years after launch in 1977. For extra credit, fans of math can calculate that at one light-day per 50 years, Voyager 1 will reach its one light-year (365 light-days) distance milestone in about 18,250 years.","img":"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/IMG_4364N_Kyriazis.jpg?w=1400&fit=clip","by":"Apostolos Kyriazis","video":false},"tle":["1 25544U 98067A   26323.84989826  .00011830  00000+0  21862-3 0  9994","2 25544  51.6318 249.7702 0007427  44.2199 315.9382 15.49496274595883"],"passes":[{"start":"2026-11-20T16:47:21Z","end":"2026-11-20T16:53:56Z","top":"2026-11-20T16:50:38Z","max":58,"from":["SW","西南"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":7},{"start":"2026-11-20T18:24:01Z","end":"2026-11-20T18:26:51Z","top":"2026-11-20T18:27:22Z","max":87,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":3},{"start":"2026-11-21T17:36:04Z","end":"2026-11-21T17:40:40Z","top":"2026-11-21T17:39:25Z","max":89,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-21T19:12:52Z","end":"2026-11-21T19:13:36Z","top":"2026-11-21T19:16:12Z","max":68,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":1},{"start":"2026-11-22T16:48:07Z","end":"2026-11-22T16:54:49Z","top":"2026-11-22T16:51:27Z","max":84,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":7},{"start":"2026-11-22T18:24:54Z","end":"2026-11-22T18:27:43Z","top":"2026-11-22T18:28:15Z","max":81,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":3},{"start":"2026-11-23T17:36:55Z","end":"2026-11-23T17:41:30Z","top":"2026-11-23T17:40:16Z","max":90,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-23T19:13:44Z","end":"2026-11-23T19:14:26Z","top":"2026-11-23T19:16:54Z","max":41,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":1}],"track":{"t0":"2026-11-20T07:43:00Z","step":60,"p":[[46.4,-163.5],[44.6,-158.9],[42.6,-154.5],[40.4,-150.5],[38.1,-146.8]